257
00:11:16.220 --> 00:11:17.300
Oh, my gosh.

258
00:11:17.540 --> 00:11:19.180
Here is what she had to say.

259
00:11:20.380 --> 00:11:26.860
So, Greg Daniels had told me that I would be able to direct an episode season nine, which

260
00:11:26.860 --> 00:11:29.980
I was really excited about, but I didn't know which episode.

261
00:11:29.980 --> 00:11:37.040
When I got the script for Customer Loyalty and I read it, I absolutely could not believe

262
00:11:37.040 --> 00:11:42.040
that Greg had given me the script where we revealed the documentary crew for the very

263
00:11:42.040 --> 00:11:47.280
first time, because I was a new director, and that just seemed unbelievably huge.

264
00:11:47.280 --> 00:11:52.980
So, I started at the beginning of the script, and I just kind of worked my way through it.

265
00:11:53.160 --> 00:11:54.840
I spent a lot of time on stage.

266
00:11:54.840 --> 00:12:00.400
I spent a lot of time looking at angles and talking to Matt Sohn, our DP, about how to

267
00:12:00.400 --> 00:12:05.180
stage things so that they'd be funny and so they'd be interesting and look like it belonged

268
00:12:05.180 --> 00:12:05.780
in our show.

269
00:12:06.440 --> 00:12:10.800
If I had gotten this script as a first-time director, I would have pooped my pants and

270
00:12:10.800 --> 00:12:11.540
handed it back.

271
00:12:11.720 --> 00:12:12.040
I know.

272
00:12:12.300 --> 00:12:13.800
And, like, hard pass.

273
00:12:13.800 --> 00:12:18.500
This is the same thing we talked about with Bryan Cranston, is you say yes, but then you

274
00:12:18.500 --> 00:12:20.060
don't know the episode you're going to get.

275
00:12:20.560 --> 00:12:21.940
This was a huge episode.

276
00:12:21.940 --> 00:12:24.180
It had a bunch of toddlers.

277
00:12:24.400 --> 00:12:24.640
Yep.

278
00:12:25.340 --> 00:12:27.680
It had this major reveal.

279
00:12:27.940 --> 00:12:29.420
It had multiple locations.

280
00:12:30.100 --> 00:12:30.520
Yeah.

281
00:12:30.800 --> 00:12:35.260
Well, I'll tell you from my point of view, because I had been working as a producer this

282
00:12:35.260 --> 00:12:41.100
season, I knew this was coming, so it was really fun for me to sit in that table read and have

283
00:12:41.100 --> 00:12:42.400
everybody else find out.

284
00:12:43.100 --> 00:12:48.440
But this storyline of Pam being comforted by the boom operator was actually a pitch from

285
00:12:48.440 --> 00:12:51.440
Mindy Kaling that went all the way back to season three.

286
00:12:51.720 --> 00:12:52.460
Oh, wow.

287
00:12:52.920 --> 00:12:53.080
Yeah.

288
00:12:53.220 --> 00:12:58.400
And I remember Greg bringing it up to me and John over the summer during our producer

289
00:12:58.400 --> 00:12:59.960
sessions for season nine.

290
00:12:59.980 --> 00:13:03.860
So I reached out to Greg because I wanted to kind of get this backstory.

291
00:13:04.160 --> 00:13:05.700
And here's what Greg said.

292
00:13:05.880 --> 00:13:10.760
Greg said, yes, it was originally a pitch for Pam when she was in New York going to art

293
00:13:10.760 --> 00:13:11.080
school.

294
00:13:11.080 --> 00:13:16.400
The idea was that she was on the subway and she was getting hassled by someone and the

295
00:13:16.400 --> 00:13:19.960
boom operator would drop his boom mic and come in to save her.

296
00:13:20.560 --> 00:13:24.540
And once he was revealed, he would become a little bit of a character on the show.

297
00:13:25.160 --> 00:13:27.460
Maybe she would have a few meals with him.

298
00:13:27.640 --> 00:13:32.940
The idea was that we wanted to make people worry that she was maybe drifting apart from

299
00:13:32.940 --> 00:13:34.240
Jim while she was in New York.

300
00:13:35.100 --> 00:13:38.700
Greg said it was pretty much the story role that Rich Sommer ended up playing.

301
00:13:39.200 --> 00:13:44.040
And he said he loved this idea and everyone in the writers room loved this idea, but they

302
00:13:44.040 --> 00:13:45.980
felt like it was something we should save for later.

303
00:13:46.200 --> 00:13:47.600
Kind of like what you were saying, Angela.

304
00:13:48.180 --> 00:13:53.080
He said it kind of made you think about the documentary crew too much for like a season

305
00:13:53.080 --> 00:13:53.960
three moment.

306
00:13:54.180 --> 00:13:55.260
Yeah, that's too soon.

307
00:13:55.260 --> 00:13:55.760
I agree.

308
00:13:55.760 --> 00:13:59.680
He said it would be hard to put that back in the bottle for the rest of the season.

309
00:13:59.900 --> 00:14:00.960
Yeah, because you're like, what?

310
00:14:01.060 --> 00:14:02.140
Is the guy standing there?

311
00:14:02.360 --> 00:14:04.500
Yes, you'd be thinking about them too much.

312
00:14:05.240 --> 00:14:08.020
But Greg said he always thought it was a really creative pitch.

313
00:14:08.140 --> 00:14:13.100
And he said, but considering it was season nine and he was aiming at the documentary airing

314
00:14:13.100 --> 00:14:17.120
at the end of season nine, he said, we wouldn't need to put anything back in the bottle.

315
00:14:17.840 --> 00:14:19.640
So they could go with this.

316
00:14:20.080 --> 00:14:24.680
And he said, you know, remember we discussed putting a little conflict between Pam and Jim

317
00:14:24.680 --> 00:14:27.420
for season nine because we didn't want it to be all smooth sailing.

318
00:14:28.120 --> 00:14:32.600
And so he said, Jim was going to go to Philly, kind of like Pam going to New York.

319
00:14:32.740 --> 00:14:37.820
And this was an opportunity for some drama and tension so that the eventual happy ending

320
00:14:37.820 --> 00:14:38.920
would feel even better.

321
00:14:38.920 --> 00:14:44.620
However, he wants fans to know there was never any way that he wasn't going to give Jim and

322
00:14:44.620 --> 00:14:45.840
Pam a happy ending.

323
00:14:46.540 --> 00:14:50.280
But the boom operator seemed like something that would worry the audience.

324
00:14:50.880 --> 00:14:57.120
And he said, it was really the only plausible relationship that Pam could have had all these

325
00:14:57.120 --> 00:15:01.880
years that we wouldn't know anything about because the crew's never been included in the

326
00:15:01.880 --> 00:15:02.220
footage.

327
00:15:03.120 --> 00:15:05.880
And he said, it did worry the audience.

