00:43:55.140 --> 00:43:55.960
That lizard is here.

1028
00:43:58.380 --> 00:43:59.020
That's it.

1029
00:43:59.120 --> 00:44:00.060
I put it on your resume.

1030
00:44:00.460 --> 00:44:00.780
Can do.

1031
00:44:01.060 --> 00:44:01.860
Cute lizard.

1032
00:44:02.160 --> 00:44:07.420
Can anybody take this lizard voice and put it onto a lizard, and we'll post it on Office

1033
00:44:07.420 --> 00:44:08.320
Ladies' Pod?

1034
00:44:08.820 --> 00:44:09.980
In stories.

1035
00:44:11.580 --> 00:44:13.200
Not a feed poSt.

1036
00:44:13.540 --> 00:44:15.000
Just in stories.

1037
00:44:15.700 --> 00:44:16.880
Who are you?

1038
00:44:17.080 --> 00:44:18.240
What's your character?

1039
00:44:18.500 --> 00:44:18.880
I don't know.

1040
00:44:19.000 --> 00:44:20.160
I'm just trying to match you.

1041
00:44:20.380 --> 00:44:22.580
Are you another, like, amphibian?

1042
00:44:22.580 --> 00:44:23.540
What are you?

1043
00:44:23.700 --> 00:44:24.540
Who's that guy?

1044
00:44:25.140 --> 00:44:27.240
The voice of reason guy.

1045
00:44:28.080 --> 00:44:32.160
My character has wild ideas and has lots of enthusiasm.

1046
00:44:32.160 --> 00:44:36.220
My character doesn't always want to go with the flow.

1047
00:44:36.800 --> 00:44:37.020
No.

1048
00:44:39.030 --> 00:44:40.270
This is horrible.

1049
00:44:41.690 --> 00:44:43.710
Listen, we're not writing it, okay?

1050
00:44:43.710 --> 00:44:45.850
We're just doing the voices for it.

1051
00:44:46.150 --> 00:44:46.530
Okay.

1052
00:44:47.910 --> 00:44:49.070
We're back.

1053
00:44:49.250 --> 00:44:54.210
And Nellie and Pete and Aaron are celebrating their first real like.

1054
00:44:54.450 --> 00:44:58.910
They've got a non-fake person to like Dunder Mifflin.

1055
00:44:58.910 --> 00:44:59.290
Yeah.

1056
00:44:59.590 --> 00:45:01.230
And they are very excited.

1057
00:45:01.230 --> 00:45:02.550
They do their little handshake.

1058
00:45:02.710 --> 00:45:03.590
It's really cute.

1059
00:45:03.910 --> 00:45:06.970
And Nellie is like, oh, no.

1060
00:45:07.230 --> 00:45:08.310
What have I done?

1061
00:45:08.530 --> 00:45:08.830
Yeah.

1062
00:45:09.210 --> 00:45:13.250
She said, Andy is just starting to be nice to me, and now I've driven his girlfriend

1063
00:45:13.250 --> 00:45:14.930
into the arms of a younger man.

1064
00:45:15.310 --> 00:45:20.490
And she has CC'd Andy on all the incriminating correspondence, in which she tells them not to

1065
00:45:20.490 --> 00:45:24.610
hold back, to make sure their social media presence is hot, hot, hot.

1066
00:45:25.410 --> 00:45:25.850
Yeah.

1067
00:45:25.870 --> 00:45:28.530
She says, I did everything but unzip their pants for them.

1068
00:45:28.910 --> 00:45:30.930
And now she's on a mission to undo all of it.

1069
00:45:31.170 --> 00:45:35.970
I have to point out, in the background of Nellie's talking head, you know, we were always

1070
00:45:35.970 --> 00:45:37.410
doing background for each other.

1071
00:45:38.730 --> 00:45:40.370
Super cutesy background.

1072
00:45:40.850 --> 00:45:47.730
Like, Pete and Aaron are just continuing very animated, flirty, handshake-y cutesiness.

1073
00:45:48.470 --> 00:45:52.610
Dwight is now going to announce that he's ordering coffee for the whole team and presents

1074
00:45:52.610 --> 00:45:53.470
a sign-up sheet.

1075
00:45:53.470 --> 00:45:58.810
Phyllis looks below the top flap and discovers it's actually a loyalty pledge.

1076
00:45:58.990 --> 00:46:01.750
She's trying to be sneaky and get them to sign it.

1077
00:46:01.970 --> 00:46:07.990
Well, after this episode aired, NBC released a copy of Dwight's loyalty pledge, and here's

1078
00:46:07.990 --> 00:46:09.090
what it had to say.

1079
00:46:09.090 --> 00:46:14.690
By writing my name in the column below, I do hereby resolve to swear an oath of loyalty

1080
00:46:14.690 --> 00:46:22.250
and obedience to Dunder Mifflin and its affiliates, hereinafter, company, for life plus 10 years.

1081
00:46:22.650 --> 00:46:28.670
My loyalty and priorities will be wholly with company and no side projects or extracurricular

1082
00:46:28.670 --> 00:46:34.330
endeavors, aka moonlighting at dumb-sounding companies, including but not limited to athlete.

1083
00:46:36.070 --> 00:46:43.030
I also promise not to take tips or kickbacks or any form of payola, as such term is generally

1084
00:46:43.030 --> 00:46:47.970
defined in the radio industry, in exchange for giving special treatment to any customers,

1085
00:46:48.330 --> 00:46:49.870
hereinafter customers.

1086
00:46:50.310 --> 00:46:55.530
My devotion to the company shall be nothing less than unconditional obedience, and I shall

1087
00:46:55.530 --> 00:47:02.110
be prepared at all times to give my life, to uphold this oath in this life and the hereafter.

1088
00:47:02.870 --> 00:47:05.570
One coffee order maximum per name, no pizza.

1089
00:47:06.070 --> 00:47:08.510
And then it listed everybody's coffee order.

1090
00:47:08.770 --> 00:47:13.970
Can I just say, I feel like he had to put no pizza because it's come up before, that they've

1091
00:47:13.970 --> 00:47:17.250
had a coffee order and someone has also asked for pizza.

1092
00:47:17.690 --> 00:47:18.330
Yes.

1093
00:47:19.230 --> 00:47:23.970
All right, here is the coffee order for the folks at Dunder Mifflin.

1094
00:47:24.710 --> 00:47:26.970
Phyllis ordered a banana fruit smoothie.

1095
00:47:27.950 --> 00:47:29.990
Stanley ordered a small decaf.

1096
00:47:29.990 --> 00:47:33.510
Daryl ordered a double latte, lotsa latte.

1097
00:47:34.570 --> 00:47:39.050
Oscar ordered a venti kai, tea misto, half soy.

1098
00:47:39.890 --> 00:47:42.050
Kevin ordered a cappuccino.

1099
00:47:42.530 --> 00:47:45.530
Is that different from a cappuccino?

1100
00:47:45.610 --> 00:47:48.630
I think it's what Kevin thinks is a cappuccino.

1101
00:47:48.790 --> 00:47:50.310
He wrote, Captain Chino.

1102
00:47:51.130 --> 00:47:52.110
Okay, okay.

1103
00:47:52.410 --> 00:47:54.970
Pete ordered a cappuccino with cinnamon.

1104
00:47:56.130 --> 00:47:59.770
Clark ordered a tall and black like my women.

1105
00:48:00.790 --> 00:48:05.650
Nellie ordered a black tea, any, with lemon like my men.

1106
00:48:06.530 --> 00:48:10.950
Aaron ordered a vanilla blendy thing, five sugars, happy face.

1107
00:48:11.750 --> 00:48:14.670
Meredith ordered an Irish coffee, extra Irish.

1108
00:48:15.850 --> 00:48:18.430
And this goes to your theory, Angela.

1109
00:48:18.770 --> 00:48:22.350
Creed ordered a pastrami on rye, fries, Coke, nothing to drink.

1110
00:48:22.690 --> 00:48:22.970
Mm-hmm.

1111
00:48:23.670 --> 00:48:24.110
Yeah.

1112
00:48:24.410 --> 00:48:25.130
There you go.

1113
00:48:25.550 --> 00:48:26.910
Angela did not order any.

1114
00:48:27.150 --> 00:48:28.370
No, she didn't.

1115
00:48:29.550 --> 00:48:33.670
Angela Martin and Angela Kinsey don't want to be part of your coffee order.

1116
00:48:33.930 --> 00:48:35.890
Angela Martin does not want to be stimulated.

1117
00:48:36.510 --> 00:48:36.830
Mm-mm.

1118
00:48:37.690 --> 00:48:38.690
She doesn't.

1119
00:48:38.970 --> 00:48:40.750
And Angela Kinsey doesn't drink coffee.

1120
00:48:40.870 --> 00:48:42.490
And Angela Kinsey doesn't drink coffee.

1121
00:48:43.290 --> 00:48:45.850
Dwight now bursts into the annex and he says,

1122
00:48:46.090 --> 00:48:50.190
Clark, I need any complaints pertaining to Daryl in the past few weeks.

1123
00:48:50.330 --> 00:48:53.050
I want it broken down by keywords.

1124
00:48:53.330 --> 00:48:56.030
And Clark's like, listen, that's going to be tough.

1125
00:48:56.190 --> 00:48:57.250
We use Windows 95.

1126
00:48:58.090 --> 00:49:00.070
And Dwight's like, fine, just print it out.

1127
00:49:00.410 --> 00:49:04.030
Then this cuts to that hilarious dot matrix printer.

1128
00:49:04.030 --> 00:49:07.230
That's like, kee, kee, kee, kee.

1129
00:49:07.490 --> 00:49:08.810
Yeah, it's going to take forever.

1130
00:49:09.170 --> 00:49:13.310
And when we asked Kelly Cantley what memory she had from shooting this episode,

1131
00:49:13.530 --> 00:49:15.370
this was one of the scenes she mentioned.

1132
00:49:15.650 --> 00:49:16.430
Here's what she said.

1133
00:49:17.270 --> 00:49:23.830
The scene where Dwight goes into Clark and tells him to print all the complaints.

1134
00:49:24.770 --> 00:49:29.970
I looked and looked at that scene and I could not figure out how it was going to be funny

1135
00:49:29.970 --> 00:49:31.370
until we shot it.

1136
00:49:31.370 --> 00:49:38.270
And Matt's own brilliant operator dropped the camera down to just over the machine

1137
00:49:38.270 --> 00:49:40.690
onto Dwight and Clark.

1138
00:49:40.970 --> 00:49:43.550
And then I thought it was just so funny.

1139
00:49:43.730 --> 00:49:45.630
It makes me laugh every time I see it.

1140
00:49:46.110 --> 00:49:51.190
I think this scene is so funny because it is the callback to Clark

1141
00:49:52.070 --> 00:49:56.530
being frustrated by our just dinosaur technology.

1142
00:49:56.530 --> 00:49:58.430
Yeah, talk about old tech.

1143
00:49:58.730 --> 00:50:00.450
He's surrounded by old tech.

1144
00:50:01.370 --> 00:50:04.810
Dwight is now going to hold a conference room meeting about customer loyalty.

1145
00:50:05.150 --> 00:50:05.830
What is it?

1146
00:50:06.010 --> 00:50:07.250
Can you hold it in your hand?

1147
00:50:07.610 --> 00:50:08.890
Can you dump it on a woman?

1148
00:50:09.310 --> 00:50:10.910
No, because it's an idea.

1149
00:50:11.170 --> 00:50:12.370
What does it mean?

1150
00:50:12.670 --> 00:50:16.310
This whole time a man has been sitting at the front of the conference room,

1151
00:50:16.390 --> 00:50:19.870
Dwight is now going to introduce him as Mr. Romanko,

1152
00:50:19.870 --> 00:50:24.590
a client of 20 years who came in today enraged at Daryl,

1153
00:50:24.710 --> 00:50:27.970
who was distracted because he was working on outside projects.

1154
00:50:28.130 --> 00:50:31.890
And Mr. Romanko is like, no, no, no, I wouldn't classify this as rage.

1155
00:50:32.030 --> 00:50:33.410
He seems a bit confused.

1156
00:50:33.670 --> 00:50:36.490
Well, there was a scene that would have come previous to this

1157
00:50:36.490 --> 00:50:39.350
that sort of explains it all and set up the whole scene.

1158
00:50:39.530 --> 00:50:41.510
In the shooting draft, it read like this.

1159
00:50:41.510 --> 00:50:45.910
A client, Mr. Romanko, a meek little man, enters the office tentatively.

1160
00:50:46.450 --> 00:50:47.390
Dwight spots him.

1161
00:50:47.750 --> 00:50:51.970
Dwight says, Mr. Romanko, right away, so sorry you felt the need to come in.

1162
00:50:52.190 --> 00:50:54.470
Mr. Romanko says, I didn't.

1163
00:50:54.550 --> 00:50:57.450
You called, but it's such a small matter.

1164
00:50:57.610 --> 00:50:59.470
Maybe we should just, Dwight says, I understand,

1165
00:50:59.490 --> 00:51:02.290
but we take customer loyalty very seriously here.

1166
00:51:03.070 --> 00:51:05.410
Emergency conference room meeting, everyone.

1167
00:51:05.750 --> 00:51:07.430
Mr. Romanko is like confused.

1168
00:51:07.670 --> 00:51:08.090
He's like, what?

1169
00:51:08.270 --> 00:51:10.130
And he turns to Mr. Romanko and says,

1170
00:51:10.130 --> 00:51:12.670
I hope you have nothing planned for the whole afternoon.

1171
00:51:13.670 --> 00:51:17.030
And Mr. Romanko says, actually, I do have.

1172
00:51:17.150 --> 00:51:19.990
And Dwight pushes Romanko into the conference room

1173
00:51:19.990 --> 00:51:23.790
and then shouts to everyone, irate customer coming through.

1174
00:51:24.550 --> 00:51:24.850
Yes.

1175
00:51:25.070 --> 00:51:27.270
When we get back to the conference room,

1176
00:51:27.430 --> 00:51:29.570
Daryl is going to say, I'm so sorry.

1177
00:51:29.570 --> 00:51:31.970
We were a day late on your delivery,

1178
00:51:31.970 --> 00:51:34.470
but two of our trucks were down for repairs

1179
00:51:34.470 --> 00:51:36.810
and I don't see this ever happening again.

1180
00:51:36.810 --> 00:51:40.050
And Mr. Romanko is like, fine, great.

1181
00:51:40.050 --> 00:51:41.370
He's satisfied with that answer.

1182
00:51:41.470 --> 00:51:42.290
He wants to leave.

1183
00:51:42.590 --> 00:51:43.750
Yeah, he's like, good for me.

1184
00:51:44.250 --> 00:51:46.870
Dwight's like, no, Mr. Romanko is angry.

1185
00:51:47.070 --> 00:51:50.670
And Daryl forgot that loyalty is the key to relationships.

1186
00:51:51.410 --> 00:51:53.790
Well, Nellie is going to be like, I agree.

1187
00:51:54.150 --> 00:51:54.670
Yes.

1188
00:51:54.790 --> 00:51:57.630
She sees her way out now and she's going to take it.

1189
00:51:57.830 --> 00:52:00.010
She says loyalty is everything.

1190
00:52:00.270 --> 00:52:02.170
And they should all ask themselves

1191
00:52:02.170 --> 00:52:05.030
if they've been faithful in their relationships.

1192
00:52:05.790 --> 00:52:07.290
Stanley is like, uh-uh,

1193
00:52:07.570 --> 00:52:09.530
he's not going to participate in this conversation.

1194
00:52:10.110 --> 00:52:12.530
Nellie says Daryl is dating Dunder Mifflin,

1195
00:52:12.670 --> 00:52:14.870
but flirting with athlete on the side.

1196
00:52:15.090 --> 00:52:19.150
Then they start using Aaron as an example.

1197
00:52:19.390 --> 00:52:21.430
Like, what would it be like

1198
00:52:21.430 --> 00:52:25.090
if Aaron, who is in a relationship with Andy,

1199
00:52:25.270 --> 00:52:27.450
was flirting with someone on the side,

1200
00:52:27.610 --> 00:52:28.870
like maybe Creed?

1201
00:52:29.350 --> 00:52:30.550
And Creed's lying.

1202
00:52:30.750 --> 00:52:31.370
He's so funny.

1203
00:52:31.370 --> 00:52:33.390
He's like, yeah, I'll play that out.

1204
00:52:33.870 --> 00:52:35.390
He's like, sure, yeah, let's see what,

1205
00:52:35.870 --> 00:52:36.810
let's play that out.

1206
00:52:36.990 --> 00:52:39.190
And imagine during all of this,

1207
00:52:39.390 --> 00:52:42.290
poor Mr. Romanko is just like, can I go?

1208
00:52:42.990 --> 00:52:46.310
And this conference room scene was so fun to shoot.

1209
00:52:46.470 --> 00:52:49.030
We broke and laughed several times.

1210
00:52:49.230 --> 00:52:51.790
And I loved this little brief exchange

1211
00:52:51.790 --> 00:52:53.070
between Angela and Aaron.

1212
00:52:53.070 --> 00:52:53.950
I want to play it.

1213
00:52:54.490 --> 00:52:55.910
Well, I think it would be immoral

1214
00:52:55.910 --> 00:52:57.370
for Aaron to cheat on Andy.

1215
00:52:57.530 --> 00:52:58.090
Oh, I'm sorry.

1216
00:52:58.370 --> 00:52:59.530
Didn't you cheat on Andy?

1217
00:52:59.530 --> 00:53:01.590
Yes, and he didn't like it.

1218
00:53:04.220 --> 00:53:05.000
That too.

1219
00:53:05.220 --> 00:53:06.680
I love when you said, yes,

1220
00:53:06.820 --> 00:53:08.340
and he didn't like it very much.

1221
00:53:08.460 --> 00:53:09.620
Yes, and I'm really put out,

1222
00:53:09.700 --> 00:53:10.600
and he didn't like it.

1223
00:53:11.620 --> 00:53:13.540
One of our favorite things as a cast,

1224
00:53:13.560 --> 00:53:14.620
we've talked about this before,

1225
00:53:14.840 --> 00:53:16.440
is to have a big group scene

1226
00:53:16.440 --> 00:53:18.140
where everyone has a moment.

1227
00:53:18.140 --> 00:53:20.280
And this was one of those scenes.

1228
00:53:20.560 --> 00:53:21.660
Everyone in the conference room

1229
00:53:21.660 --> 00:53:23.920
had something hilarious that they contributed.

1230
00:53:24.860 --> 00:53:27.960
And by the way, Mr. Romanko was great.

1231
00:53:28.420 --> 00:53:31.000
Yes, guest star, shout out to Mr. Romanko,

1232
00:53:31.120 --> 00:53:32.240
played by Bob Bluberman.

1233
00:53:32.340 --> 00:53:34.920
He was originally a lawyer who left law

1234
00:53:34.920 --> 00:53:36.740
to become an actor in 1995.

1235
00:53:37.280 --> 00:53:38.940
Well, Bob has crossover connections

1236
00:53:38.940 --> 00:53:39.880
with both you and I.

1237
00:53:39.960 --> 00:53:40.540
You want to hear them?

1238
00:53:40.760 --> 00:53:41.100
Yes.

1239
00:53:41.400 --> 00:53:43.140
Bob and I have both had roles

1240
00:53:43.140 --> 00:53:45.120
on Spin City and Strong Medicine.

1241
00:53:45.800 --> 00:53:47.980
And Angela, your crossover connections

1242
00:53:47.980 --> 00:53:50.060
are Hot in Cleveland, New Girl,

1243
00:53:50.200 --> 00:53:51.400
and Fresh Off the Boat.

1244
00:53:51.560 --> 00:53:54.040
Bob, we've worked on so many of the same shows.

1245
00:53:54.280 --> 00:53:54.680
I know.

1246
00:53:54.860 --> 00:53:57.100
He's appeared in over 100 TV shows,

1247
00:53:57.520 --> 00:53:58.520
dozens of commercials,

1248
00:53:58.880 --> 00:54:01.160
and voiceover spots.

1249
00:54:01.380 --> 00:54:01.840
Bob.

1250
00:54:01.980 --> 00:54:02.840
Hook us up.

1251
00:54:02.980 --> 00:54:03.240
Yeah.

1252
00:54:03.500 --> 00:54:04.560
We have so many voices.

1253
00:54:04.880 --> 00:54:06.100
We can do a lot.

1254
00:54:06.380 --> 00:54:07.680
Hey, now, listen, Bob.

1255
00:54:07.800 --> 00:54:08.800
I got this guy, too.

1256
00:54:09.000 --> 00:54:09.820
I can do this one.

1257
00:54:09.960 --> 00:54:11.300
He works at a tire shop.

1258
00:54:11.880 --> 00:54:12.780
Tim's Tire Town.

1259
00:54:12.780 --> 00:54:14.660
I always say,

1260
00:54:14.860 --> 00:54:16.860
if you're going to get your beauty done,

1261
00:54:17.040 --> 00:54:18.220
get your beauty done right.

1262
00:54:19.040 --> 00:54:20.060
That's what she says.

1263
00:54:20.460 --> 00:54:20.880
See?

1264
00:54:21.060 --> 00:54:21.560
Look at us.

1265
00:54:21.660 --> 00:54:21.780
Bob.

1266
00:54:22.200 --> 00:54:23.360
What can't we do?

1267
00:54:23.460 --> 00:54:23.740
Bob.

1268
00:54:24.860 --> 00:54:25.740
Probably voiceover.

1269
00:54:27.620 --> 00:54:29.000
Well, should we head on over

1270
00:54:29.000 --> 00:54:30.180
to Cece's Recital?

1271
00:54:30.180 --> 00:54:31.620
Because it is underway.

1272
00:54:32.520 --> 00:54:33.560
Yes, it is.

1273
00:54:33.580 --> 00:54:35.020
And I have a few more things

1274
00:54:35.020 --> 00:54:36.400
to share about this day.

1275
00:54:37.220 --> 00:54:38.260
Kelly had made sure

1276
00:54:38.260 --> 00:54:39.340
I had the day off,

1277
00:54:39.360 --> 00:54:40.940
so when we filmed these scenes,

1278
00:54:40.960 --> 00:54:41.580
I could be there

1279
00:54:41.580 --> 00:54:42.540
just right off camera.

1280
